exports[`git.grove.list given: [case1] a forest of a hetzner row, an ec2 row, a relic, and a corrupt row when: [t1] it is listed with the probe then: the probe reads as a snapshot 1`] = `
"🌲 forest
   ├─ 🌳 grove-sandpine-corrupt → 🟡 row unreadable — its fix is named above
   ├─ 🌳 grove-sandpine-hetzner-v20261022 → camper@127.0.0.2:1 (ssh:grove-sandpine-hetzner-v20261022)
   │     ├─ 🔴 DOWN — no ssh banner: refused — the box answers; no sshd on this port
   │     └─ fix → the box answered on 1 and refused — is sshd up there, and is 1 its port? (a stale ssm-era port reads this way; re-register — git grove set grove-sandpine-hetzner-v20261022 --at camper@127.0.0.2:22)
   ├─ 🌳 grove-sandpine-hetzner-v20261023 → camper@grove-sandpine-hetzner-v20261023.invalid:22 (ssh:grove-sandpine-hetzner-v20261023)
   │     ├─ 🔴 DOWN — no ssh banner: the name is unknown to dns — is it a tailnet peer?
   │     └─ fix → check the tailnet — tailscale status (is this machine a peer?), then tailscale ping grove-sandpine-hetzner-v20261023.invalid
   ├─ 🌳 grove-sandpine-v20250101 → camper@grove-sandpine-v20250101.invalid:22 (ssh:grove-sandpine-v20250101)
   │     ├─ 🔴 DOWN — no ssh banner: the name is unknown to dns — is it a tailnet peer?
   │     └─ fix → wake it — rhx git.grove.wake grove-sandpine-v20250101
   └─ 🌳 grove-sandpine-v20260901 → camper@grove-sandpine-v20260901.invalid:22 (ssh:grove-sandpine-v20260901)
         ├─ 🔴 DOWN — no ssh banner: the name is unknown to dns — is it a tailnet peer?
         └─ fix → wake it — rhx git.grove.wake grove-sandpine-v20260901

🛟 a grove did not greet with ssh — each row names its cure, by the cause it saw.
   first, if every row reads DOWN, is THIS machine a peer? — tailscale status
🛟 a row is unreadable — re-register it with the fix named above, then list again
"
`;

